      <div type="clause" n="62.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 62.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 62.1" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="583" ed="#liebermann"/>Ab Aduentu Domini usque ad octabas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.2"/> Epiphanie et a<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.3"/> Septuagesima usque ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.4"/> XV dies post Pascha<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.5"/> et festis diebus et Quatuor temporum et diebus Quadragesimalibus et aliis legittimis ieiuniis et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.6"/> in diebus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.a"/> Ueneris et uigiliis sanctorum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.7"/> Apostolorum non est tempus leges faciendi, id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.8"/> est uel iusiurandum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.9"/> pro<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.10"/> fidelitate domini uel concordia[m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.11"/>] uel bellum uel ferri uel aque uel alias<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.12"/> legis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.13"/> examinaciones tractari;</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 583 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Summa leg. Norm. 80: Sunt tempora in quibus leges non debent fieri nec simplices nec aperte, uidelicet omnia tempora in quibus matrimonium non potest celebrari. Ecclesia autem legibus apparentibus omnes dies treuge ecclesiastice prohibet ac defendit, uidelicet ab hora nona in die Iouis usque ad ortum solis in die Lune subsequente et dies IX lectionum ieiuniorum, Quatuor temporum. <hi rend="italic">Hn steht zwischen diesem weitgehenden Gottesfrieden und Cnut, während</hi> E Cf. 2 <hi rend="italic">die Treuga erst Sonnabend Mittag beginnt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Summa leg. Norm. 80: Sunt tempora in quibus leges non debent fieri nec simplices nec aperte, uidelicet omnia tempora in quibus matrimonium non potest celebrari. Ecclesia autem legibus apparentibus omnes dies treuge ecclesiastice prohibet ac defendit, uidelicet ab hora nona in die Iouis usque ad ortum solis in die Lune subsequente et dies IX lectionum ieiuniorum, Quatuor temporum. Hn stands between this far-reaching Truce of God and Cnut, whereas in E Cf. 2 the Treuga begins only at noon on Saturday</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-bis <hi rend="italic">Or; umgestellt aus</hi> E. o. <hi rend="italic">Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-bis Or; transposed from E. o. Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ad LXX <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ad LXX Sc Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Wh</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in Wh</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-am <hi rend="italic">Wh Wi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-am Wh Wi</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">singulorum <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">singulorum Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">idem <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> i. e. <hi rend="italic">K Co Or Gi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">idem instead of i. e. K Co Or Gi</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iur. <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg ohne</hi> ius</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iur. Sc Hg without ius</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nisi primo <hi rend="italic">K Co Or Gi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nisi primo K Co Or Gi</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ia <hi rend="italic">Hss.; gebessert Wi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ia MSS; emended by Wi</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K Co Or Gi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in K Co Or Gi</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">583</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">leges examinationis <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">leges examinationis Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_62-1.lnote.oe._" n="-" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Freitag 1f.; Eid 9; Mannschaftseid 1; Schiedsgericht 3a; Gerichtsferien—am Rande spät: <hi rend="italic">Quibus temporibus nemo iurare cogitur in curia</hi>—<hi rend="italic">singulorum</hi>{7} vielleicht besser—<hi rend="italic">idem</hi>{8} <hi rend="italic">uel i. nisi p</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">alias</hi>{12} fehlt—<hi rend="italic">leges</hi>{13} <hi rend="italic">examinacionis</hi>—62, 2 <hi rend="italic">p. ante</hi>{15}—62, 3a <hi rend="italic">revertantur</hi> Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Freitag 1f.; Eid 9; Mannschaftseid 1; Schiedsgericht 3a; Gerichtsferien—in the margin, in a late hand: <hi rend="italic">Quibus temporibus nemo iurare cogitur in curia</hi>—<hi rend="italic">singulorum</hi>{7} perhaps better—<hi rend="italic">idem</hi>{8} <hi rend="italic">uel i. nisi p</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">alias</hi>{12} missing—<hi rend="italic">leges</hi>{13} <hi rend="italic">examinacionis</hi>—62, 2 <hi rend="italic">p. ante</hi>{15}—62, 3a <hi rend="italic">revertantur</hi> Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
